    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-006",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The volume \\(V(x)\\) in cubic inches of the open-top box is a function of the side length \\(x\\) in inches of the square cutouts. Make a plan to figure out how to construct the box with the largest volume.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-007",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Pause here so your teacher can review your plan.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-008",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Write an expression for \\(V(x)\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-009",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Use graphing technology to create a graph representing \\(V(x)\\). Approximate the value of \\(x\\) that would allow you to construct an open-top box with the largest volume possible from one piece of paper.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-010",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The surface area \\(A(x)\\) in square inches of the open-top box is also a function of the side length \\(x\\) in inches of the square cutouts.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-011",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Find one expression for \\(A(x)\\) by summing the area of the five faces of our open-top box.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-012",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Find another expression for \\(A(x)\\) by subtracting the area of the cutouts from the area of the paper.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Show algebraically that these two expressions are equivalent.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Polynomials can be used to model lots of situations. One example is to model the volume of a box created by removing squares from each corner of a rectangle of paper.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Let \\(V(x)\\) be the volume of the box in cubic inches where \\(x\\) is the side length in inches of each square removed from the four corners.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "To define \\(V\\) using an expression, we can use the fact that the volume of a cube is \\((length)(width)(height)\\). If the piece of paper we start with is 3 inches by 8 inches, then:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle V(x) = (3-2x)(8-2x)(x)\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What are some reasonable values for \\(x\\)? Cutting out squares with side lengths less than 0 inches doesn’t make sense, and similarly, we can’t cut out squares larger than 1.5 inches, since the short side of the paper is only 3 inches…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "By graphing this function, it is possible to find the maximum value within a specific domain. Here is a graph of \\(y=V(x)\\). It looks like the largest volume we can get for a box made this way from a 3 inch by 8 inch piece of paper is…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L01-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Building the Biggest Box",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A polynomial function of \\(x\\) is a function given by a sum of terms, each of which is a constant times a whole number power of \\(x\\). The word polynomial is used to refer both to the function and to the expression defining it.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
